Programs shipped in platform packages (bin/<platform>/)
-------------------------------------------------------
- wisp-helper: the FSDB/WCZ reader, distributed as a prebuilt binary (its source is not part of this repository),
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Ansh Tulsyan. It reads FSDB files with its own decoder; it contains no Synopsys/Verdi code
  and loads no vendor library. Statically linked: zstd's decompressor (BSD-3-Clause), zlib (Zlib licence) and the
  LLVM C++ runtime (libc++, libc++abi, libunwind; Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception). bin/<platform>/wisp-helper.buildinfo
  names its build id, target and toolchain.
- cmux-sv-model (when a platform package ships it prebuilt): the design model for driver tracing, built from
  media/cmux/sv-model/ (GPL-3.0-or-later) on slang 12.1 (MIT) with fmt (MIT), Boost.Regex (BSL-1.0) and
  toml++ (MIT). Without a prebuilt copy it is built on first use from the same sources (see media/cmux/sv-model/
  build.sh, which keeps slang's notice).

Verdi
-----
No Synopsys/Verdi file is part of this extension. Verdi-based features (the optional Verdi cross-check in Trace
Driver) run the user's own Verdi installation, under the user's own Verdi licence, and start only when the user asks.

